    {
      "name": "upcoming",
      "kind": "event",
      "figures": ["events", "calendars", "occurrences", "guests", "reminders"],
      "description": "Non-cancelled events, soonest first, with the calendars they could land on, each event's calendar_id, link, reminders, its attachments and its guest list (each `{party_id, name, partstat, is_you}`, read from the event's attendee edges). Defaults to today forward; pass ISO `from`/`to` instants to read any visible range (month and week views do), including still-running multi-day events that began before `from`. A repeating event (rule set) is materialized into one row per occurrence inside the visible range, each carrying the series' real event_id, an `instance_key` for list render and the `original_start_local` an occurrence edit is keyed on; a skipped day is left out and a moved one is where it moved to. Every occurrence also carries where it falls in the request's `tz`.",
